-- Azure SQL Database Compute Models
	A. vCore-Based Model - Allocates a configurable number of virtual cores (vCores), memory, and storage resources for the database.
	B. DTU-Based Model - Uses Database Transaction Units (DTUs), an abstracted measure combining CPU, memory, and I/O to define performance.
	C. Serverless Compute - Automates scaling and pauses databases when idle, billing per second of usage.
-- Service Tiers
	General Purpose: Balanced, budget-oriented workloads with built-in storage redundancy.
	Business Critical: High-performance workloads requiring low-latency I/O and high resilience with multiple replicas.
	Hyperscale: Maximized for high throughput, massive storage, rapid backup/restore, and horizontal scaling for OLTP or HTAP workloads.

